# GSAP animated sites

When creating or refining scroll/hero/UI animations in this repo:

1. **Use MCP `gsap-master` first** (tools from [gsap-master-mcp-server](https://github.com/bruzethegreat/gsap-master-mcp-server)):
   - `understand_and_create_animation` — new motion from natural language
   - `get_gsap_api_expert` — API / plugin docs
   - `generate_complete_setup` — framework setup (prefer React)
   - `debug_animation_issue` — lag, ScrollTrigger, mobile
   - `optimize_for_performance` — 60fps / mobile
   - `create_production_pattern` — hero, scroll systems, text, transitions
2. Optional: `annnimate` for extra GSAP patterns if useful.
3. Adapt output to **this codebase** — do not paste vanilla/Next boilerplate blindly.

## Project conventions

- Library: `gsap` + `ScrollTrigger` (already in `package.json`).
- Prefer a hook like `useLandingGsap(rootRef)` with `useLayoutEffect` + `gsap.context(..., root)` + cleanup `ctx.revert()`.
- Mark targets with `data-lp='...'` (or similar data attrs), not fragile class-only selectors.
- Wrap motion in `gsap.matchMedia()` + `(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.
- Ship **2–3 intentional motions** per surface (hero timeline, section reveals, one signature effect) — not noise.
- Prefer `autoAlpha` over `opacity`; use `power2/power3` easings; scrub/pin only when it clarifies hierarchy.
- Desktop-only pins via nested `matchMedia("(min-width: 768px)")`.
- Align with existing landing design rules (brand-first hero, no card clutter in hero).
